<title>NETHERLANDS: FORECAST - DUTCH COMPANY RESULTS DUE JAN 13.</title>
<headline>FORECAST - DUTCH COMPANY RESULTS DUE JAN 13.</headline>
<dateline>AMSTERDAM 1997-01-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Analysts' estimates of Dutch</p>
<p>company results for week beginning Monday, Jan 13 include:</p>
<p>DATE--COMPANY-------PERIOD--PFT/DIV--CONSENSUS--RANGE-----PVS</p>
<p> 13/01 Randstad	YR 96     PFT     202.7   196.2-210   163.3</p>
<p> 14/01 Ahrend	  YR 96     PFT	40.8	38-43.5   33.5</p>
<p> 16/01 OPG  1st half 96/97     PFT	30.0    28.7-34     34</p>
<p>Profit figures are net profits before extraordinary items</p>
<p>and in millions of guilders unless otherwise stated.</p>
<p>Securities houses surveyed included: Amstgeld, Bangert</p>
<p>Pontier, BZW, Delta Lloyd Bank, Generale Bank, Gilissen, ING</p>
<p>Bank, Kempen &amp; Co, Lanschot Bankiers, Mees Pierson, NIB</p>
<p>Strating, Wesselius and Wijs &amp; Van Oostveen.</p>
<p>NOTE - Banks and brokers interested in contributing to</p>
<p>Reuters surveys can contact the Amsterdam newsroom on</p>
<p>+31-20-504-5000 or fax their forecasts to +31-20-504 5040.</p>
<p>For the week starting January 20 we are collecting year</p>
<p>result forecast for ASM Litho.</p>
<p>Amsterdam newsroom, +31 20 504 5000 (FAX 31-20-504-5040)</p>
</text>
